<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Halfaya</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Halfaya al-Muluk, Halfayat al-Muluk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Halfaya, or Halfayat al-Muluk, is a town on the east bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> north of the confluence of the Blue and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-nile">White Niles</a>, now part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khartoum">Khartoum</a> North in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>. In the later Funj period it became the seat of the Abdallab shaykhs, the chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/funj-sultanate-of-sennar">Sennar</a>, who had earlier ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qerri">Qerri</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/halfaya.jpg" alt="Halfaya" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ayham.Alkasim · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D9%85%D8%AF%D9%8A%D9%86%D8%A9_%D8%AD%D9%84%D9%81%D8%A7%D9%8A%D8%A7.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
